        "name": "Vācaspati Miśra",
        "text": "Articulates the methodological superiority of the Naiyāyika position. Realism about wholes respects the deliverance of perception; Buddhist atomism overrides perception in favor of metaphysical theory. The former is more epistemically conservative."
